# The two figures below ARE committed, deliberately, despite being generated:
#
#   sst_vs_folger_four_panel.png  <- make_comparison.py
#   preview_compare_points.png    <- preview_compare_points.py
#
# They were ignored at first, on the reasoning that both rebuild offline in seconds and
# a ~450 kB PNG rewritten on every run is the history bloat data/README.md warns about.
# That reasoning was wrong about the audience: the figure IS the deliverable here, and
# requiring a reviewer to run the folder before they can see what it produces is a worse
# cost than the bytes. Reviewed on GitHub, they render inline.
#
# The bloat concern is real but bounded: this folder is not on a refresh workflow (the
# ONC exports are static), so these change only when someone re-downloads inputs.
# If that stops being true, ignore them again rather than letting every run add a MB.

# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#   ../folger_compare_points.geojson   the layer the map app consumes. Committed for the
#                                      same reason sst_barkley_layer.geojson is -- the
#                                      app reads it from main, and a consumer should
#                                      never have to run this folder to get it.
